2025-07-11 11:59:46,341 - INFO - Raw band profile response: Band Name: Echoes of the Mirage  
Author Style: In the style of Lester Bangs  
Nationality: Australian  
Genre 1: Psychedelic Rock  
Genre 2: Ethereal Wave  
Style Name: Dreamy Dissonance  
Reference Year: 1973  

Echoes of the Mirage emerges from the sun-soaked shores of Australia, carving out a soundscape that is as mesmerizing as a desert mirage. Their music is a kaleidoscopic journey through the vast outback of the mind, where the echoes of the past meet the shimmering possibilities of the future. With a style they aptly dub "Dreamy Dissonance," they effortlessly blend the mind-bending riffs of Psychedelic Rock with the hauntingly beautiful whispers of Ethereal Wave.

In the year 1973, a time when the world was teetering on the edge of change, Echoes of the Mirage captured the zeitgeist with their debut album, sending ripples through the music scene. Their sound is a lush tapestry woven from the threads of surreal guitar effects, reverb-drenched vocals, and hypnotic rhythms that transport listeners to a realm where reality and illusion dance in a harmonious embrace. As Lester Bangs might have mused, they are the aural equivalent of a dream within a dream—intangible yet profoundly resonant.
